$comment
ERROR EXAMPLE: Impossible charge/multiplicity combination.
Water (10 electrons) declared as neutral doublet (0,2). An even number of
electrons cannot give multiplicity 2.
Q-Chem error: "Inconsistent number of electrons / multiplicity" /
WAVEFUNCTION_INCONSISTENT.
Fix: use (0,1) for neutral singlet, or (-1,2)/(+1,2) for a radical ion.
$end

$molecule
0 2
O   0.000000   0.000000   0.117300
H   0.000000   0.756950  -0.469200
H   0.000000  -0.756950  -0.469200
$end

$rem
   JOBTYPE         opt
   METHOD          b3lyp
   BASIS           6-31G*
   UNRESTRICTED    true
$end

@@@

$molecule
   READ
$end

$rem
   JOBTYPE         freq
   METHOD          b3lyp
   BASIS           6-31G*
   UNRESTRICTED    true
$end
